  <section id="opening-preferences">
    <title>Opening preferences</title>
    <p>
      Use the commands below to open the global or application Preferences window.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also run <code>orca -s</code> or <code>orca --setup</code> in a terminal or your
      desktop's Run dialog to start Orca and open the Preferences window. If Orca is already
      running, this opens its Preferences window instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      Application preferences override global preferences for that application. For example, you
      can use different speech settings in your browser and text editor.
    </p>
    <section id="commands-opening-preferences">
      <title>Commands</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>Commands</gui> category, <gui>Commands</gui> section, <gui>Screen Reader Management</gui> group.
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Display the preferences window</gui>
            <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Space</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>Display the application preferences window</gui>
            <keyseq>
              <key>Orca Modifier</key>
              <key>Ctrl</key>
              <key>Space</key>
            </keyseq>
          </p>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
