  <section id="changing-and-saving-settings">
    <title>Changing and saving settings</title>
    <p>
      Settings are grouped into categories in the side panel on the left. Use <key>Up Arrow</key> and <key>Down Arrow</key> to choose a category. As you
      change categories, the panel on the right displays that category's settings. Press <key>Tab</key> to move into that panel.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some categories contain subcategories. Use <key>Up Arrow</key> and <key>Down Arrow</key> to choose one, then <key>Right Arrow</key> or <key>Enter</key> to open it. Press <key>Left Arrow</key> or <key>Escape</key> to return to the subcategory list.
      From the main settings list, press <key>Left Arrow</key> to return to the sidebar. Use <key>Tab</key> and <keyseq>
        <key>Shift</key>
        <key>Tab</key>
      </keyseq>
      to move among controls.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Options menu button is at the top of the left panel. Press <key>F10</key> to move to Options. You can also
      reach it from the sidebar with <keyseq>
        <key>Shift</key>
        <key>Tab</key>
      </keyseq>. Press <key>Enter</key> or <key>Space</key> to open the menu. Use the Options
      menu's apply action to save your changes without closing the window, or its save action to
      save and close it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Options menu's Cancel action closes the window and discards unsaved preference edits.
      Changes already applied remain saved.
    </p>
    <p>
      Preferences is a window, not a dialog: <key>Escape</key> does not close it. Close it with <keyseq>
        <key>Alt</key>
        <key>F4</key>
      </keyseq>
      or the Options menu. If you press <keyseq>
        <key>Alt</key>
        <key>F4</key>
      </keyseq>
      with unsaved changes, Orca prompts you to save them, close without saving, or cancel and
      return to preferences. In global preferences, you can also save the changes as a new
      profile.
    </p>
  </section>
